    "name": "Shiitake Mushrooms",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">The stems of the shiitake mushroom are stringier and harder than the cap, and you can cut off the bottom half of the stem - or the entire stem - to make the mushrooms easier to eat. Slice the mushrooms into thin strips and scatter them over a salad or a plate of fresh nachos for extra nutrition and a boost in flavor.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Grown by CK Fiber in Creswell OR</span></p>",
